SUMMARY:The Denver Fair
DESCRIPTION:The Denver Fair is a vibrant\, five-day community tradition held annually in mid-September at Denver Memorial Park in Lancaster County\, Pennsylvania. Established in 1981 by local volunteers\, this non-profit event has maintained free admission since 1983\, attracting over 40\,000 visitors. \nThe fair celebrates the region’s agricultural roots with livestock shows\, competitive exhibits for baked goods\, and unique contests like hot wing eating or the baby parade. Families can enjoy a bustling midway featuring nearly 30 amusement rides\, classic fair foods\, and free nightly entertainment. The festivities traditionally conclude on Saturday night with a grand fireworks display. \nThe 2026 Denver Fair is scheduled for September 15 – 19. \n\nSee our schedule of Fairs & Festivals in Lancaster County and surrounding areas.\nOther Things To Do in Lancaster\, PA\n\n\nArt Galleries\nDistilleries\nEscape Rooms\nFactory Tours\n\n\n\nIndoor Things To Do\nMassage and Spas\nOutdoor Things To Do\n\n\n\nShooting Ranges\nTheaters\nWineries\nAll Things To Do in Lancaster
URL:https://lancasterpa.com/events-calendar/the-denver-fair/
LOCATION:Denver Memorial Park\, 801 Main St\, Denver\, 17517\, United States
CATEGORIES:Adamstown,Children & Family Events,Entertainment,Ephrata, PA,Fairs & Festivals,Food & Beverage Events
